# INBOX-79 commit 7A residual audit and hard enforcement

Commit 7A audits the accepted commit-6 code state `324fa993` from the
docs-only dispatch HEAD `627de956`. No production emitter source, canary tool,
mandatory runner, build step, or Tier-3 infrastructure changed.

The historical per-file maximum-count guard was replaced by two exact,
function-scoped allowlists:

- 48 residual accumulator operation groups / 72 occurrences covering every
  production consumer `bindEax`, `bindRax`, `bindAccumulator`,
  `clobberAccumulator`, and `bindValueLoc` site;
- 8 predeclared pair/RDX exclusion groups / 11 occurrences covering the urem
  RDX result, fixed full-product RAX/RDX, and every current pair-result bind.

Every entry records file, enclosing function, operation, structural role,
classification, future architectural slice, and exact expected occurrence
count. The audit found zero unclassified sites and no ordinary EAX/RAX result
producer outside `AccumulatorDefinitionTransaction`. Full enumeration:
[INBOX-79 residual audit](inbox79_residual_accumulator_audit.md).

The guard fails closed on:

- an added operation in an otherwise allowlisted function;
- relocation to a different function;
- operation reclassification (clobber changed to bind);
- removal/count drift;
- an approved pair/RDX exclusion without the owning
  `pair_rdx_authority` future slice.

